{
 "thread": "M4druK6_FTs",
 "subject": "Is there any syntactic sugar for using debounce/throttle on an input value?",
 "messages_listed": 4,
 "last_activity": "2017-08-02T22:07:52Z",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "NaYvJm3mAAAJ",
   "from": "Dean Attali",
   "author": "a1bf76ab9a5a2d4b",
   "date": "2017-08-02T20:28:17Z",
   "subject": "Is there any syntactic sugar for using debounce/throttle on an input value?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Suppose I have a numeric input with ID &quot;num&quot; and in the server I want to refer to `input$num`. I want it to fire no more than once every second, so I want to use the `throttle(r, 1000)` function.<div><br></div><div>This is the code I would:</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">num </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> reactive</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">input$num</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>num_t </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> throttle</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">num</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>observe</span><span style=\"color:#660\">({</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  cat</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">num_t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">())</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">})</span></div></code></div><font color=\"#000000\" style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\"><br></span><span><br></span></font></div><div>I was wondering if there&#39;s a more compact way to do this, without having to define a variable that only gets used in one place?<br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "j01E3ArsBAAJ",
   "from": "Joe Cheng",
   "author": "ca443e6eaa0e78ed",
   "date": "2017-08-02T21:07:20Z",
   "subject": "Re: Is there any syntactic sugar for using debounce/throttle on an input value?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Is this what you mean?<div><br></div><div>num &lt;- reactive(input$num) %&gt;% throttle(1000)</div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
